; Tutorial 5.03: Menus and Requesters
;
; A small text editor, with what nearly every program on a desktop has: a menu bar, keys like Ctrl+S that do the same
; as a menu item, a window that asks for the name of a file, and a question before unsaved work is lost.
;
; A window gets a menu bar from the style flag BB_WINDOW_MENU. WindowMenu gives the bar, and CreateMenu adds the menus
; to it and the items to the menus. Each item has a number of its own, chosen by the program. When an item is
; picked, WaitEvent returns BB_EVENT_MENU and EventData is that number. After changing the menus, UpdateWindowMenu
; shows the changes.
;
; Requesters are the small windows that ask the user something: RequestFile for the name of a file, RequestFont for
; a font, Notify for a message, Confirm for yes or no, and Proceed for yes, no or cancel. The program waits until the
; user has answered.
;
; New things here:
;   CreateMenu, WindowMenu, UpdateWindowMenu, CheckMenu, UncheckMenu and MenuChecked.
;   HotKeyEvent, which turns a key with Ctrl into the same event as a menu item.
;   CreateTextArea, TextAreaText and SetTextAreaText.
;   RequestFile, RequestFont, Notify and Proceed.
;   Reading and writing a text file line by line, from tutorial 1.11, now with a window around it.
;
; Keys: Ctrl+N new, Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+S save, Ctrl+Q quit.

Include "<gui.bb>"

; The numbers of the menu items. Any numbers will do, as long as each item has its own.
Const MENU_NEW = 1, MENU_OPEN = 2, MENU_SAVE = 3, MENU_SAVE_AS = 4, MENU_QUIT = 5
Const MENU_FONT = 10, MENU_STATUS = 11, MENU_ABOUT = 20

Const TITLE$ = "Tutorial 5.03: Notes"

; Flags 1 title bar, 2 resizable, 4 menu bar, 8 status bar.
Global window = CreateWindow(TITLE, 100, 80, 560, 420, 0, BB_WINDOW_TITLEBAR + BB_WINDOW_RESIZABLE + BB_WINDOW_MENU + BB_WINDOW_STATUS)
SetMinWindowSize window, 300, 200

; The text area fills the whole inside of the window, and SetGadgetLayout keeps it that way when the window changes
; its size: all four edges keep their distance to the sides of the window.
Global area = CreateTextArea(0, 0, ClientWidth(window), ClientHeight(window), window)
SetGadgetLayout area, BB_EDGE_ALIGNED, BB_EDGE_ALIGNED, BB_EDGE_ALIGNED, BB_EDGE_ALIGNED

; --- The menus -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; CreateMenu takes the text, the number of the item, and the menu it goes in. The menus on the bar get 0 as their
; number, since picking them only opens them. An item with an empty text is a line between items. The & in front of a
; letter marks it as the key that opens the menu together with Alt.
Local bar = WindowMenu(window)
Local fileMenu = CreateMenu("&File", 0, bar)
CreateMenu "&New" + Chr(9) + "Ctrl+N", MENU_NEW, fileMenu
CreateMenu "&Open..." + Chr(9) + "Ctrl+O", MENU_OPEN, fileMenu
CreateMenu "&Save" + Chr(9) + "Ctrl+S", MENU_SAVE, fileMenu
CreateMenu "Save &as...", MENU_SAVE_AS, fileMenu
CreateMenu "", 0, fileMenu
CreateMenu "&Quit" + Chr(9) + "Ctrl+Q", MENU_QUIT, fileMenu

Local viewMenu = CreateMenu("&View", 0, bar)
CreateMenu "&Font...", MENU_FONT, viewMenu
; This item can have a tick in front of it, set with CheckMenu and read with MenuChecked.
Global statusItem = CreateMenu("&Count the characters", MENU_STATUS, viewMenu)
CheckMenu statusItem

Local helpMenu = CreateMenu("&Help", 0, bar)
CreateMenu "&About", MENU_ABOUT, helpMenu
UpdateWindowMenu window

; --- Keys ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; HotKeyEvent makes a key into an event of the program's choice. The first number is the key (the same numbers as
; KeyHit uses), the second the keys held with it: 1 Shift, 2 Ctrl, 4 Alt. Making Ctrl+S send the event of the Save
; item means that the code below needs to handle it only once.
HotKeyEvent 49, 2, BB_EVENT_MENU, MENU_NEW
HotKeyEvent 24, 2, BB_EVENT_MENU, MENU_OPEN
HotKeyEvent 31, 2, BB_EVENT_MENU, MENU_SAVE
HotKeyEvent 16, 2, BB_EVENT_MENU, MENU_QUIT

; --- What the editor knows -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Global fileName$ = ""     ; Empty while the text has never been saved.
Global changed = False    ; Whether the text changed since it was last saved or opened.
Global font = 0

SetTextAreaText area, "Write something here, then try the menus." + Chr(10) + "Ctrl+S saves, and closing the window asks first if the text was not saved."
changed = False
ShowTitle()
ActivateGadget area ; Puts the cursor into the text, so the user can start to type at once.

Repeat
	Select WaitEvent()
		Case BB_EVENT_GADGET
			; A text area sends BB_EVENT_GADGET whenever its text changes.
			If EventSource() = area
				changed = True
				ShowTitle()
			EndIf

		Case BB_EVENT_MENU
			Select EventData()
				Case MENU_NEW
					If MayDropText()
						SetTextAreaText area, ""
						fileName = ""
						changed = False
						ShowTitle()
					EndIf
				Case MENU_OPEN
					If MayDropText() Then OpenText()
				Case MENU_SAVE
					SaveText(False)
				Case MENU_SAVE_AS
					SaveText(True)
				Case MENU_QUIT
					If MayDropText() Then Exit
				Case MENU_FONT
					PickFont()
				Case MENU_STATUS
					ToggleStatusBar()
				Case MENU_ABOUT
					Notify "Notes, a small text editor." + Chr(10) + Chr(10) + "Tutorial 5.03 of BlitzLLVM."
			End Select

		Case BB_EVENT_WINDOW_CLOSE
			If MayDropText() Then Exit
	End Select
Forever

If font Then FreeFont font
End

; The title shows the name of the file, and a * while there are unsaved changes, like many editors do.
Function ShowTitle()
	Local name$ = fileName
	If name = "" Then name = "Untitled"
	If changed Then name = name + " *"
	SetGadgetText window, name + " - " + TITLE
	If MenuChecked(statusItem) Then SetStatusText window, Len(TextAreaText(area)) + " characters"
End Function

; Before the text is thrown away: if it has changes, ask whether to save them. Proceed answers 1 for yes, 0 for no
; and -1 for cancel. True means that the text may go.
Function MayDropText()
	If Not changed Then Return True
	Select Proceed("The text has changes that were not saved. Save them first?")
		Case 1
			Return SaveText(False)
		Case 0
			Return True
	End Select
	Return False
End Function

; Saves the text. True if it was saved, False if the user cancelled the requester.
Function SaveText(askName)
	Local name$ = fileName
	If askName Or name = ""
		; The third number of RequestFile says that it asks for a file to save, not to open. The filter "txt" shows
		; only text files.
		name = RequestFile("Save the text as", "txt", True, "notes.txt")
		If name = "" Then Return False
	EndIf

	Local file = WriteFile(name)
	If file = 0
		Notify "Could not write " + name + ".", True
		Return False
	EndIf
	; A text area keeps its lines apart with Chr(13), the "carriage return", like the text boxes of Windows do. Each
	; line is written with WriteLine, which ends it the way text files on the computer end their lines.
	Local text$ = TextAreaText(area), start = 1, found
	Repeat
		found = Instr(text, Chr(13), start)
		If found = 0
			WriteLine file, Mid(text, start)
			Exit
		EndIf
		WriteLine file, Mid(text, start, found - start)
		start = found + 1
	Forever
	CloseFile file

	fileName = name
	changed = False
	ShowTitle()
	Return True
End Function

Function OpenText()
	Local name$ = RequestFile("Open a text", "txt", False)
	If name = "" Then Return
	Local file = ReadFile(name)
	If file = 0
		Notify "Could not read " + name + ".", True
		Return
	EndIf
	; ReadLine gives each line without its end, so the lines are joined again with Chr(13).
	Local text$ = "", lines = 0
	While Not Eof(file)
		If lines > 0 Then text = text + Chr(13)
		text = text + ReadLine(file)
		lines = lines + 1
	Wend
	CloseFile file

	SetTextAreaText area, text
	fileName = name
	changed = False
	ShowTitle()
End Function

; RequestFont shows the fonts of the computer and gives back the one that was picked, already loaded, or 0 if the user
; cancelled. SetGadgetFont uses it for the text area.
Function PickFont()
	Local picked = RequestFont()
	If picked = 0 Then Return
	SetGadgetFont area, picked
	If font Then FreeFont font
	font = picked
	SetStatusText window, "Font: " + FontName(font) + ", " + FontSize(font)
End Function

; Picking the item turns its tick on or off. While it is on, the status bar counts the characters of the text.
Function ToggleStatusBar()
	If MenuChecked(statusItem)
		UncheckMenu statusItem
		SetStatusText window, ""
	Else
		CheckMenu statusItem
	EndIf
	UpdateWindowMenu window
	ShowTitle()
End Function
